-- ccc13-wreck-stores.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part X: sections 415 to 421 (wreck, public stores, military uniforms and stores).
-- Reading of the answers as in ccc13-fraud.l4. The section 2 terms "wreck" and "public stores" are called with the keel's own inputs.

§ `Part X -- sections 415 to 421`

§§ `Wreck -- section 415`

-- 415 Every one who (a) secretes wreck, defaces or obliterates the marks on wreck or uses any means to disguise or conceal the fact that anything is wreck, or in any manner conceals the character of wreck, from a person who is entitled to inquire into the wreck,
-- (b) receives wreck, knowing that it is wreck, from a person other than the owner thereof or a receiver of wreck, and does not within forty-eight hours thereafter inform the receiver of wreck thereof,
-- (c) offers wreck for sale or otherwise deals with it, knowing that it is wreck, and not having a lawful authority to sell or deal with it,
-- (d) keeps wreck in his possession knowing that it is wreck, without lawful authority to keep it, for any time longer than the time reasonably necessary to deliver it to the receiver of wreck, or
-- (e) boards, against the will of the master, a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress unless he is a receiver of wreck or a person acting under orders of a receiver of wreck, is guilty of (f) an indictable offence ... two years, or (g) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:7455 | Wreck
-- src:7456 | Offences in relation to wreck
-- src:7457 | 415 Every one who
-- src:7458 | (a) secretes wreck, defaces or obliterates the marks on wreck or uses any means to disguise or conceal the fact that anything is wreck, or in any manner conceals the character of wreck, from a person who is entitled to inquire into the wreck,
-- src:7459 | (b) receives wreck, knowing that it is wreck, from a person other than the owner thereof or a receiver of wreck, and does not within forty-eight hours thereafter inform the receiver of wreck thereof,
-- src:7460 | (c) offers wreck for sale or otherwise deals with it, knowing that it is wreck, and not having a lawful authority to sell or deal with it,
-- src:7461 | (d) keeps wreck in his possession knowing that it is wreck, without lawful authority to keep it, for any time longer than the time reasonably necessary to deliver it to the receiver of wreck, or
-- src:7462 | (e) boards, against the will of the master, a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress unless he is a receiver of wreck or a person acting under orders of a receiver of wreck,
-- src:7463 | is guilty of
-- src:7464 | (f) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or
-- src:7465 | (g) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 415 (src:7455-7465)
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `s 2 wreck kind`
      `the person secretes wreck, defaces or obliterates the marks on wreck, uses any means to disguise or conceal the fact that anything is wreck, or in any manner conceals the character of wreck` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the concealment is from a person who is entitled to inquire into the wreck` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(a) the conduct is the offence of concealing wreck` MEANS
    IF `the person secretes wreck, defaces or obliterates the marks on wreck, uses any means to disguise or conceal the fact that anything is wreck, or in any manner conceals the character of wreck` AND `the concealment is from a person who is entitled to inquire into the wreck`
    THEN `s 2 wreck` `what the thing is`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE if the thing is not wreck (NOTHING if s 2 wreck leaves it open)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) secretes wreck, defaces or obliterates the marks on wreck"

-- (b) ... does not within forty-eight hours thereafter inform the receiver of wreck thereof: a period the text fixes in its own words.
-- Informed within forty-eight hours (inclusive) is the text's no. Still inside the period and not yet informed is, on the same words, an element not yet met: JUST FALSE (fork F10).
@ref s 415(b) (src:7459-7459)
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `s 2 wreck kind`
      `the person receives wreck, knowing that it is wreck, from a person other than the owner thereof or a receiver of wreck` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours since the person received the wreck` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours after receipt at which the person informed the receiver of wreck, if the person has done so` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person receives wreck, knowing that it is wreck, from a person other than the owner thereof or a receiver of wreck`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) receives wreck, knowing that it is wreck, from a person other than the owner thereof or a receiver of wreck"
    ELSE IF CONSIDER `the hours after receipt at which the person informed the receiver of wreck, if the person has done so`
            WHEN JUST informed THEN informed GREATER THAN 48
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the hours since the person received the wreck` GREATER THAN 48
         THEN `s 2 wreck` `what the thing is`
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not within forty-eight hours thereafter inform the receiver of wreck thereof"

@ref s 415(c) (src:7460-7460)
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `s 2 wreck kind`
      `the person offers wreck for sale or otherwise deals with it, knowing that it is wreck` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has no lawful authority to sell or deal with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(c) the conduct is the offence of dealing with wreck without lawful authority` MEANS
    IF `the person offers wreck for sale or otherwise deals with it, knowing that it is wreck` AND `the person has no lawful authority to sell or deal with it`
    THEN `s 2 wreck` `what the thing is`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) offers wreck for sale or otherwise deals with it, knowing that it is wreck, and not having a lawful authority to sell or deal with it"

@ref s 415(d) (src:7461-7461)
GIVEN `what the thing is` IS A `s 2 wreck kind`
      `the person keeps wreck in their possession knowing that it is wreck, without lawful authority to keep it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person keeps it for longer than the time reasonably necessary to deliver it to the receiver of wreck` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(d) the conduct is the offence of keeping wreck` MEANS
    IF `the person keeps wreck in their possession knowing that it is wreck, without lawful authority to keep it` AND `the person keeps it for longer than the time reasonably necessary to deliver it to the receiver of wreck`
    THEN `s 2 wreck` `what the thing is`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) keeps wreck in his possession knowing that it is wreck, without lawful authority to keep it, for any time longer than the time reasonably necessary to deliver it to the receiver of wreck"

-- (e) boards, against the will of the master, a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress unless he is a receiver of wreck or a person acting under orders of a receiver of wreck.
-- "unless" once met is decided case by case (the maintainer, 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE, fork F6.
@ref s 415(e) (src:7462-7463)
GIVEN `the person boards, against the will of the master, a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a receiver of wreck or a person acting under orders of a receiver of wreck` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415(e) the conduct is the offence of boarding a wrecked vessel` MEANS
    IF `the person is a receiver of wreck or a person acting under orders of a receiver of wreck`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he is a receiver of wreck or a person acting under orders of a receiver of wreck"
    ELSE IF `the person boards, against the will of the master, a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) boards, against the will of the master, a vessel that is wrecked, stranded or in distress"

@ref s 415 (the offence, any of its paragraphs) (src:7455-7465)
GIVEN `the person commits the offence of paragraph (a), by s 415(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits the offence of paragraph (b), by s 415(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits the offence of paragraph (c), by s 415(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits the offence of paragraph (d), by s 415(d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits the offence of paragraph (e), by s 415(e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 415 the person is guilty of an offence in relation to wreck` MEANS
    `ccc13 any of` (LIST `the person commits the offence of paragraph (a), by s 415(a)`, `the person commits the offence of paragraph (b), by s 415(b)`, `the person commits the offence of paragraph (c), by s 415(c)`, `the person commits the offence of paragraph (d), by s 415(d)`, `the person commits the offence of paragraph (e), by s 415(e)`)
    -- JUST FALSE when every paragraph is JUST FALSE: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who"

@ref s 415 (the punishments) (src:7455-7465)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 415 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 415 (the class of the offence) (src:7455-7465)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 415 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§§ `Public Stores -- sections 416 to 421`

-- (3) For the purposes of this section, distinguishing mark means a distinguishing mark that is appropriated for use on public stores pursuant to section 416.
-- Section 416 is the Governor in Council's power to prescribe the marks by notice (machinery): whether a mark has been appropriated is the fact asked here.
-- src:7478 | Definition of distinguishing mark
-- src:7479 | (3) For the purposes of this section, distinguishing mark means a distinguishing mark that is appropriated for use on public stores pursuant to section 416.
@ref s 417(3) (src:7478-7479)
GIVEN `the mark is appropriated for use on public stores pursuant to section 416` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 417(3) the mark is a distinguishing mark` MEANS
    IF `the mark is appropriated for use on public stores pursuant to section 416`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "distinguishing mark means a distinguishing mark that is appropriated for use on public stores pursuant to section 416"

-- (1) Every person ... who, (a) without lawful authority applies a distinguishing mark to anything, or (b) with intent to conceal the property of Her Majesty in public stores, removes, destroys or obliterates, in whole or in part, a distinguishing mark.
-- src:7470 | Applying or removing marks without authority
-- src:7471 | 417 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who,
-- src:7472 | (a) without lawful authority applies a distinguishing mark to anything, or
-- src:7473 | (b) with intent to conceal the property of Her Majesty in public stores, removes, destroys or obliterates, in whole or in part, a distinguishing mark.
@ref s 417(1) (src:7470-7473)
GIVEN `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person applies the mark to anything` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to conceal the property of Her Majesty in public stores` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person removes, destroys or obliterates, in whole or in part, the mark` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mark is a distinguishing mark, by s 417(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 417(1) the conduct is the offence of applying or removing a distinguishing mark` MEANS
    IF    (`the person acts without lawful authority` AND `the person applies the mark to anything`)   -- (a)
       OR (`the person acts with intent to conceal the property of Her Majesty in public stores` AND `the person removes, destroys or obliterates, in whole or in part, the mark`)   -- (b)
    THEN `the mark is a distinguishing mark, by s 417(3)`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who,"

@ref s 417(1) (the punishments) (src:7470-7473)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 417(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 417(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7470-7473)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 417(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (2) Every person who, without lawful authority, receives, possesses, keeps, sells or delivers public stores that they know bear a distinguishing mark is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... two years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:7474 | Unlawful transactions in public stores
-- src:7475 | (2) Every person who, without lawful authority, receives, possesses, keeps, sells or delivers public stores that they know bear a distinguishing mark is guilty of
-- src:7476 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:7477 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 417(2) (src:7474-7477)
GIVEN `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receives, possesses, keeps, sells or delivers the stores` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stores are personal property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stores are under the care, supervision, administration or control of a public department or of any person in the service of a public department` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the stores bear a distinguishing mark` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mark is a distinguishing mark, by s 417(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 417(2) the conduct is the offence of unlawful transactions in public stores` MEANS
    IF `the person acts without lawful authority` AND `the person receives, possesses, keeps, sells or delivers the stores` AND `the person knows that the stores bear a distinguishing mark`
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `s 2 public stores` `the stores are personal property` `the stores are under the care, supervision, administration or control of a public department or of any person in the service of a public department`
                            , `the mark is a distinguishing mark, by s 417(3)`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, without lawful authority, receives, possesses, keeps, sells or delivers public stores that they know bear a distinguishing mark"

@ref s 417(2) (the punishments) (src:7474-7477)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 417(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 417(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7474-7477)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 417(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- 418 (1) Every one who knowingly sells or delivers defective stores to Her Majesty or commits fraud in connection with the sale, lease or delivery of stores to Her Majesty or the manufacture of stores for Her Majesty is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
-- src:7480 | Selling defective stores to Her Majesty
-- src:7481 | 418 (1) Every one who knowingly sells or delivers defective stores to Her Majesty or commits fraud in connection with the sale, lease or delivery of stores to Her Majesty or the manufacture of stores for Her Majesty is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 418(1) (src:7480-7481)
GIVEN `the person knowingly sells or delivers defective stores to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person commits fraud in connection with the sale, lease or delivery of stores to Her Majesty or the manufacture of stores for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 418(1) the conduct is the offence of selling defective stores to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly sells or delivers defective stores to Her Majesty` OR `the person commits fraud in connection with the sale, lease or delivery of stores to Her Majesty or the manufacture of stores for Her Majesty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who knowingly sells or delivers defective stores to Her Majesty or commits fraud in connection with the sale, lease or delivery of stores to Her Majesty or the manufacture of stores for Her Majesty"

@ref s 418(1) (the punishments) (src:7480-7481)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 418(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 418(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7480-7481)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 418(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- (2) Every one who, being a representative of an organization that commits, by fraud, an offence under subsection (1), (a) knowingly takes part in the fraud, or
-- (b) knows or has reason to suspect that the fraud is being committed or has been or is about to be committed and does not inform the responsible government, or a department thereof, of Her Majesty, is guilty of an indictable offence ... fourteen years.
-- src:7482 | Offences by representatives
-- src:7483 | (2) Every one who, being a representative of an organization that commits, by fraud, an offence under subsection (1),
-- src:7484 | (a) knowingly takes part in the fraud, or
-- src:7485 | (b) knows or has reason to suspect that the fraud is being committed or has been or is about to be committed and does not inform the responsible government, or a department thereof, of Her Majesty,
-- src:7486 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 418(2) (src:7482-7486)
GIVEN `the person's place in the organization` IS A `s 2 representative: the person's place in the organization`
      `the body is an organization, by s 2 organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the organization commits, by fraud, an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly takes part in the fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows or has reason to suspect that the fraud is being committed or has been or is about to be committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person informs the responsible government, or a department thereof, of Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 418(2) the conduct is the offence of a representative of an organization taking part in fraud on Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the organization commits, by fraud, an offence under subsection (1)` AND (   `the person knowingly takes part in the fraud`   -- (a)
                                                                                  OR (`the person knows or has reason to suspect that the fraud is being committed or has been or is about to be committed` AND NOT `the person informs the responsible government, or a department thereof, of Her Majesty`))   -- (b)
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `s 2 representative` `the person's place in the organization`, `the body is an organization, by s 2 organization`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "being a representative of an organization that commits, by fraud, an offence under subsection (1)"

@ref s 418(2) (the punishments) (src:7482-7486)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 418(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 418(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7482-7486)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 418(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- 419 Every person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, without lawful authority, (a) wears a uniform of the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force or a uniform that is so similar ... that it is likely to be mistaken therefor,
-- (b) wears a distinctive mark relating to wounds received or service performed in war, or a military medal, ribbon, badge, chevron or any decoration or order ..., (c) has in his possession a certificate of discharge ... that has not been issued to and does not belong to him, or
-- (d) has in his possession a commission or warrant or a certificate ... issued to an officer or a person in or who has been in the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force, that contains any alteration that is not verified by the initials of the officer who issued it, or ...
-- src:7487 | Unlawful use of military uniforms or certificates
-- src:7488 | 419 Every person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, without lawful authority,
-- src:7489 | (a) wears a uniform of the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force or a uniform that is so similar to the uniform of any of those forces that it is likely to be mistaken therefor,
-- src:7490 | (b) wears a distinctive mark relating to wounds received or service performed in war, or a military medal, ribbon, badge, chevron or any decoration or order that is awarded for war services, or any imitation thereof, or any mark or device or thing that is likely to be mistaken for any such mark, medal, ribbon, badge, chevron, decoration or order,
-- src:7491 | (c) has in his possession a certificate of discharge, certificate of release, statement of service or identity card from the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force that has not been issued to and does not belong to him, or
-- src:7492 | (d) has in his possession a commission or warrant or a certificate of discharge, certificate of release, statement of service or identity card, issued to an officer or a person in or who has been in the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force, that contains any alteration that is not verified by the initials of the officer who issued it, or by the initials of an officer thereto lawfully authorized.
@ref s 419 (src:7487-7492)
GIVEN `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wears a uniform of the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force, or a uniform so similar that it is likely to be mistaken therefor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wears a distinctive mark relating to wounds received or service performed in war, or a military medal, ribbon, badge, chevron or any decoration or order awarded for war services, or any imitation or thing likely to be mistaken for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has in their possession a certificate of discharge, certificate of release, statement of service or identity card from the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force that has not been issued to and does not belong to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has in their possession a commission, warrant, certificate of discharge, certificate of release, statement of service or identity card, issued to an officer or a person in or who has been in the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force, that contains any alteration that is not verified by the initials of the officer who issued it, or by the initials of an officer lawfully authorized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 419 the conduct is the offence of unlawful use of military uniforms or certificates` MEANS
    IF    `the person acts without lawful authority`
      AND (   `the person wears a uniform of the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force, or a uniform so similar that it is likely to be mistaken therefor`   -- (a)
           OR `the person wears a distinctive mark relating to wounds received or service performed in war, or a military medal, ribbon, badge, chevron or any decoration or order awarded for war services, or any imitation or thing likely to be mistaken for it`   -- (b)
           OR `the person has in their possession a certificate of discharge, certificate of release, statement of service or identity card from the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force that has not been issued to and does not belong to them`   -- (c)
           OR `the person has in their possession a commission, warrant, certificate of discharge, certificate of release, statement of service or identity card, issued to an officer or a person in or who has been in the Canadian Forces or any other naval, army or air force, that contains any alteration that is not verified by the initials of the officer who issued it, or by the initials of an officer lawfully authorized`)   -- (d)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, without lawful authority,"

