-- (2) No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section where he establishes that he did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores ... were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave was accountable to Her Majesty.
-- src:7497 | Exception
-- src:7498 | (2) No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section where he establishes that he did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores in respect of which the offence was committed were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave was accountable to Her Majesty.
@ref s 420(2) (src:7497-7498)
GIVEN `the person establishes that they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave was accountable to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 420(2) the person is saved from conviction of an offence under section 420` MEANS
    IF `the person establishes that they did not know and had no reason to suspect that the military stores were owned by Her Majesty or were military stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave was accountable to Her Majesty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section where he establishes that he did not know and had no reason to suspect"; this subsection gives no defence on these facts

-- 420 (1) Every one who buys, receives or detains from a member of the Canadian Forces or a deserter or an absentee without leave therefrom any military stores that are owned by Her Majesty or for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave is accountable to Her Majesty is guilty of (a) ... five years; or (b) summary conviction.
-- src:7493 | Military stores
-- src:7494 | 420 (1) Every one who buys, receives or detains from a member of the Canadian Forces or a deserter or an absentee without leave therefrom any military stores that are owned by Her Majesty or for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave is accountable to Her Majesty is guilty of
-- src:7495 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:7496 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 420(1) (src:7493-7496)
GIVEN `the person buys, receives or detains military stores from a member of the Canadian Forces or from a deserter or an absentee without leave therefrom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stores are owned by Her Majesty or are stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave is accountable to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defence applies, by s 420(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 420(1) the conduct is the offence of buying military stores` MEANS
    IF `the person buys, receives or detains military stores from a member of the Canadian Forces or from a deserter or an absentee without leave therefrom` AND `the stores are owned by Her Majesty or are stores for which the member, deserter or absentee without leave is accountable to Her Majesty`
    THEN `ccc13 not` `the defence applies, by s 420(2)`   -- JUST FALSE when the defence applies; NOTHING carried
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who buys, receives or detains from a member of the Canadian Forces or a deserter or an absentee without leave therefrom any military stores"

@ref s 420(1) (the punishments) (src:7493-7496)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 420(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 420(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7493-7496)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 420(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- 421 (1) In proceedings under sections 417 to 420, evidence that a person was at any time performing duties in the Canadian Forces is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that his enrolment in the Canadian Forces prior to that time was regular.
-- src:7499 | Evidence of enlistment
-- src:7500 | 421 (1) In proceedings under sections 417 to 420, evidence that a person was at any time performing duties in the Canadian Forces is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that his enrolment in the Canadian Forces prior to that time was regular.
@ref s 421(1) (src:7499-7500)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under sections 417 to 420` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that the person was at any time performing duties in the Canadian Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 421(1) the evidence is proof that the person's enrolment in the Canadian Forces prior to that time was regular` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are under sections 417 to 420`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In proceedings under sections 417 to 420"
    ELSE IF NOT `there is evidence that the person was at any time performing duties in the Canadian Forces`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection makes evidence of duties proof; where there is none it is silent
         ELSE IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection 417(2) shall be presumed to have known that the stores ... bore a distinguishing mark ... at the time the offence is alleged to have been committed if he was, at that time, in the service or employment of Her Majesty or was a dealer in marine stores or in old metals.
-- src:7501 | Presumption when accused a dealer in stores
-- src:7502 | (2) An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection 417(2) shall be presumed to have known that the stores in respect of which the offence is alleged to have been committed bore a distinguishing mark within the meaning of that subsection at the time the offence is alleged to have been committed if he was, at that time, in the service or employment of Her Majesty or was a dealer in marine stores or in old metals.
@ref s 421(2) (src:7501-7502)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with an offence under subsection 417(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was, at that time, in the service or employment of Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was, at that time, a dealer in marine stores or in old metals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 421(2) the accused is presumed to have known that the stores bore a distinguishing mark` MEANS
    IF `the accused is charged with an offence under subsection 417(2)` AND (`the accused was, at that time, in the service or employment of Her Majesty` OR `the accused was, at that time, a dealer in marine stores or in old metals`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he was, at that time, in the service or employment of Her Majesty or was a dealer in marine stores or in old metals"
